{"title":"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the smallest whole number larger than the perimeter of any triangle with a side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/46949e13e716ef5eff5152de87614a8a2a45b447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }24\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }29\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }43\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }48\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality\" title=\"Triangle Inequality\">Triangle Inequality</a> that the last side, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, fulfills <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a5605bed6df8d5c27bc6c044d77f057ebef093bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&lt;5+19=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/f/44fbe1d7d1a8adacc9a4d1dcb57a2d8e75284b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> to both sides of the inequality, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259e86786cd20c9f523dbd5f331317cb896bbbc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+5+19&lt;48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />, and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/9282da89e2c3898a089252f910f5c2ef1a3a669f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s+5+19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" /> is the perimeter of our triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a310bc21c1c148d5b7b856f20b9f1b444b222987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> is our answer.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, fulfills <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a5605bed6df8d5c27bc6c044d77f057ebef093bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&lt;5+19=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />, meaning that s&lt;24. The greatest value of s can be 23. 23+5+19 is 47. Since 48 is our nearest answer choice, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a310bc21c1c148d5b7b856f20b9f1b444b222987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.-TheNerdWhoIsNerdy.\n</p><p>minor edit by themathkidwoohooooo:\nthe greatest value of s is 24-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> represents an infinitesimal (a constant smaller than any positive number but not zero or negative. it is between the positives and 0. another way to think of it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/2/422e9e545921ad0a11e1b1bfaa3ab7e85cfda000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1} {\\infty}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />). NOT 23!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rxXHhn5PB9w\">https://youtu.be/rxXHhn5PB9w</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zUiKAoX2D_Q\">https://youtu.be/zUiKAoX2D_Q</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; wi